					"font-size": {
						"type": "number",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "text",
						"value": "PROGRAM CHANGE\n\nWire allows you to both read and write MIDI program changes.\n\nProgram changes are often used in music and lighting gear to change to different settings or start up a certain preset.  Note that program change messages are channelized so they will only affect a device on a specific MIDI channel.\n\nThe Is Program Change Node will simply output a boolean. This indicates if the incoming MIDI message is in fact a program change(true) or something else(false) like a midi note or CC message.\n\nThe Program Change node will output the incoming program change as an integer.\nNote that program changes are always integers between 0 and 127.\n\nThe Write Program Change node will write a program change upon triggering the Write inlet. The program inlet value is used as the message."
					}
				},
